5761:
Ok, one more time 
The old tube type TV's were very sensitive to outside interference. With the "Rabbit Ear" antennas that were extremely popular then, the chance of interfering with a TV within your house was really great. Ask me how I know! With today's digital  tuners (made with IC's rather than tubes, they have a better rejection to outside interference. If February of '09 (not really that far away),  all sets will HAVE to have a digital tuner of some sort. ALL new sets have them built in. The older sets will need an external tuner. These tuners will NOT be able to receive the analog signal that our Bally / Astrocade units transmit. In conclusion, the small amount of "transmission" from an uncovered unit will be of no consequence to anyone then.
HOWEVER, if you live in an apartment building in a metropolitan area, you or your neighbors TV may still have rabbit ears on it and you could interfere with channels 2-5 with your unit until February.
Ken


