                kenn lill wrote:
> to all of you geniuses out there!!
> 
> I have somewhat of a dilemma. I want to write a cartridge type program 
> that has extensive text. Then I want to make it a .BIN file eventually. 
> This is the ONLY type of file that my programmer can accept. If I could 
> get it on an eprom, my programmer will make it into a .BIN

Ok,

You want to write a Cart program for the Bally. I presume you will be 
doing this in Z80 assembler. In which case you should use ZMAC. (On 
BallyAlley, used for all the tests/homebrew on BallyAlley)

The output of ZMAC is a .bin(Raw Machine code) file. This will load into 
MESS as a cart for testing and should be able to be burned to ROM easily.

BallyBin/AstroWav are only for 2000baud BASIC archiving.

If you're trying to make a BASICCart. Mike (I think) can help you.

Lance



